	(text_box "6502 CPU BOARD v2 - ROUGH CONNECTION SCHEMATIC (generated; connections by net label)\n\nCLOCK  (oscillator runs at 2x the CPU clock)\n  U8A (FF1): CLK1 <- OSC2X, D1 <- CLK_D = NAND(CLK, RDYS), Q1 = CLK (CPU clock), /Q1 = /CLK\n     PHI2 low  -> always goes high next OSC edge\n     PHI2 high & RDYS=1 -> falls (normal 50% clock)\n     PHI2 high & RDYS=0 -> stays high (clock stretch)\n  U8B (FF2): synchronises bus /STRETCH (pin 8) to OSC -> RDYS\n  No card pulling /STRETCH = plain divide-by-2.\n\nR/W ON THE BUS  (U9, 74ACT00)\n  U9A: /RD = NOT R/W  -> bus pin 12 (/SMEMR): low on every read cycle\n  U9B: /WR = NOT /RD  -> bus pin 11 (/SMEMW): low on every write cycle (buffered R/W)\n  U9C: CLK_D for the stretcher.  U9D spare (inputs grounded).\n  These carry no address decode - cards must qualify them with their own select.\n  Suggest 22-33R series resistors on CLK, /CLK, /RD, /WR where they leave for the bus.\n\n/DMA (bus DRQ2, pin 6) - one net, three listeners, driven only by a DMA master card:\n  -> U1 BE (pin 36): CPU floats A0-A15, D0-D7, R/W\n  -> U3 pin 2 (addr GAL): RDY = 0 while /DMA low  (so the CPU also stops)\n  -> U6 pin 13 (int GAL): BA16-BA19 tri-state, so the DMA master can drive them too\n\nRDY (U1 pin 2) - open-drain output of U3 (GAL drives low only), R6 1K pull-up\n  RDY low when IOREADY low (slow card, RDY-wait) OR /DMA low.\n  Must not be push-pull: the W65C02S drives RDY low itself when it executes WAI.\n\nMEMORY: RAM and ROM moved to the memory card (decodes A0-A15 + BA16-BA19, uses /RD, /WR, CLK).\n\nGAL FILES:  U3 = 6502_ADDR.PLD rev 02 (to write: IOen/IOr/IOw + RDY),  U6 = ISA_6502_CPU_INTERRUPT.PLD rev 02\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
